# MQTT QoS-2 session model with keepalive — used in 10_mqtt_fuzzing.ipynb
#
# Parameters (from MQTT 3.1.1):
#   K = 10 s  — keepalive window; broker disconnects after 1.5·K s of silence
#   Δ = 15 s  — retransmission timeout; client may resend PUBLISH if no PUBREC in Δ s
#   T = 60 s  — session budget
#
# Alphabet: CONNECT, PUBLISH, PUBREL, PINGREQ, DISCONNECT  (client-side only)
# Broker responses (CONNACK, PUBREC, PUBCOMP, PINGRESP) are checked in harness.py.
#
# n ≥ 4  (mandatory: CONNECT, PUBLISH, PUBREL, DISCONNECT)
# n = 5  → one extra event (PINGREQ anywhere, or one PUBLISH retransmission)
# n = 6  → two extras — can include up to 2 extra PUBLISHes
# n ≥ 7  → higher mix; traces with 3+ PUBLISHes trigger CVE-2023-28366 in Mosquitto ≤ 2.0.15

<CONNECT.<PINGREQ*>_[0,10].PUBLISH.<(PUBLISH+PINGREQ)*>_[0,15].PUBREL.<PINGREQ*>_[0,10].DISCONNECT>_[0,60]
